{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>For HaShem your Elohim is the one who walks with you.</b> We find the language of walking in this parashah in three modes. For concerning Israel it is written: ״כִּי ה׳ אֱלֹהֶיךָ הוּא הַהֹלֵךְ עִמָּךְ״ — meaning He holds you by the hand, guiding you on the path you walk. But concerning Joshua it is written: ״וַה׳ הוּא הַהֹלֵךְ לְפָנֶיךָ״, and concerning Moses it is written simply: ״וַיֵּלֶךְ מֹשֶׁה״ — with no support whatsoever. For this is like what is said of Noah, who was among those of little faith: ״אֶת הָאֱלֹהִים הִתְהַלֶּךְ נֹחַ״ (Genesis 6:9) — that he needed support to sustain him. So too concerning Israel it is written of them: ״כִּי ה׳ אֱלֹהֶיךָ הוּא הַהֹלֵךְ עִמָּךְ״ — for they needed support to sustain them in the fear of HaShem. But of Joshua it is said: ״וַה׳ הוּא הַהֹלֵךְ לְפָנֶיךָ״ — and He is ahead of him, for he did not need support to sustain him as much as Israel did. Nevertheless, he did not reach the level of the Patriarchs, of whom it is said: ״הָאֱלֹהִים אֲשֶׁר הִתְהַלְּכוּ אֲבוֹתַי לְפָנָיו״ — meaning that the Shekhinah was behind them. And to this level Moses attained, as it is said: ״וַיֵּלֶךְ מֹשֶׁה״ — meaning he walked alone with no support whatsoever, for one who walks behind HaShem has some support, but not like one who walks with HaShem. And for this reason they said (Bava Batra 75a): the face of Moses is like the face of the sun — just as the sun does not receive light from any other sphere, so Moses illuminated from his own righteousness; and Joshua is like the moon, which needs support from the light of the sun. But Israel are likened to the stars, for their light is meager — a little here, a little there — until they need very great support. And the scholars of astronomy said that what the stars complete in seventy years, the sun and the moon complete in a single day. So too the perfect ones, like Moses and Joshua, acquire their world in a single day — acquiring from perfection in one day what an average person can acquire only in seventy years, the span of an average person that HaShem has allotted to every person to acquire his perfection in; and sometimes old age has overtaken him and he does not know it."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :kli-yakar, :lang :en, :chapter 31, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:15:10.204796986Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}